# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Memory Gateway — .gitignore
# Publication safety: this project reads a PRIVATE Obsidian vault. Anything
# derived from the vault (mirrors, state dumps, logs, benchmark DBs) is PRIVATE
# and must never reach a public remote.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Python artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/

# --- Environment / secrets ---
.env
.env.*
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example
config/local_settings.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
credentials.json

# --- Databases (benchmark + SQLite WAL sidecars) ---
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
benchmark.db
benchmark.db-*

# --- Logs / run output ---
logs/
*.log
*.jsonl

# --- PRIVATE: anything derived from the user's Obsidian vault ---
# Ignore the CONTENTS of data/ rather than the directory itself: git cannot re-include a child of
# an excluded DIRECTORY, so `data/` + a later `!data/synthetic_vault/**` would silently do nothing.
# `data/*` keeps everything private by default while allowing the one documented exception below.
data/*
data/vault_mirror/
data/vault_state_before.json
# Diagnostic-script cache (scripts/_candidate_cache.py): candidate lists derived from the vault,
# regenerated on demand, worthless to anyone else.
data/cache/

# EXCEPTION: the SYNTHETIC corpus is generated by scripts/gen_synthetic_corpus.py and contains no
# personal data. It is published on purpose — it is what makes the benchmark reproducible by
# someone who does not have the author's vault, and the README promises a fresh clone runs with
# zero configuration. Without this exception that promise is false.
!data/synthetic_vault/

# --- Agent delegation / scratch output ---
.delegation/
graphify-out/
# EXCEPTION: the example corpus ships its OWN pre-built graph. Without it the hybrid retriever
# silently degrades to BM25-only for anyone who clones the repo (graph-reachable candidates
# disappear), so the published benchmark would not reproduce. Generated, contains no personal data.
!data/synthetic_vault/graphify-out/
!data/synthetic_vault/graphify-out/**
*.graphify-cache/

# --- Hermes integration homes (personal config, cache, history) ---
# Only the curated config.yaml files are published.
integrations/hermes/hermes_home/*
!integrations/hermes/hermes_home/config.yaml
integrations/hermes/hermes_bench/*
!integrations/hermes/hermes_bench/config.yaml
integrations/hermes/*/cache/
integrations/hermes/*/sessions/
integrations/hermes/*/memories/
integrations/hermes/*/logs/

# --- OS junk ---
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# --- Editor / IDE junk ---
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.nfs*

# Benchmark dataset derived from the private vault (real names, business decisions,
# personal note paths). Never publish. The synthetic questions.example.json ships instead.
benchmark/questions.json
reports/

# --- Eclipse/IDE project file ---
.project

# spikes: vendored third-party assets and screenshots are local-only
spikes/**/vendor/
spikes/**/shots/
spikes/**/node_modules/
spikes/**/run*.log
